\frametitle{Look}
\begin{itemize}
^^I^^I\item To insert a final slide with the title and final thanks, use \verb|\backmatter|.
^^I^^I\begin{itemize}
^^I^^I^^I\item The title also appears in footlines along with the author name, you can change this text with \verb|\footlinepayoff|
^^I^^I^^I\item You can remove the title from the final slide with \verb|\backmatter[notitle]|
^^I^^I\end{itemize}
^^I^^I\item The aspect ratio defaults to 16:9, and you should not change it to 4:3
^^I^^Ifor old projectors as it is inherently impossible to perfectly convert a
^^I^^I16:9 presentation to 4:3 one; spacings \emph{will} break
^^I^^I\begin{itemize}
^^I^^I^^I\item The \texttt{aspectratio} argument to the \texttt{beamer} class is
^^I^^I^^Ioverridden by the SINTEF theme
^^I^^I^^I\item If you \emph{really} know what you are doing, check the package
^^I^^I^^Icode and look for the \texttt{geometry} class.
^^I^^I\end{itemize}
^^I\end{itemize}
